{
    "background_story": "Queenie was a brilliant and pioneering engineer who dedicated her life to the field of thermography. Growing up, she was fascinated by the way heat could be used to reveal hidden patterns and secrets. She spent years studying and experimenting, eventually developing a revolutionary new technique for using thermography to detect energy inefficiencies in buildings. Her breakthrough led to a new standard in sustainable architecture, and Queenie's company became a leading consultant for eco-friendly design. As her reputation grew, so did her passion for sharing her knowledge. Queenie traveled the world, teaching and collaborating with other innovators to push the boundaries of thermography. Her work not only reduced carbon footprints but also inspired a new generation of scientists and engineers to explore the possibilities of heat-based technology.",
